  {va=0x140c4f242, old="488d04c5e43de600", new="488d04c5c8bd810b", why="upper2 extra: 0xe63de4 -> 0xb81bdc8 (lea rax, [rax*8 + 0xe63de4] in 0x140c4f0f0, whose rbx is the edit block ([owner+0x48], loaded through 0x1414b6a60 two instructions in). The block base arrives in a separate `add rax, rbx` after the lea, so the lea on its own shows no block reference and the attribution walk never filed it. It is the base of a 30000-entry 8-byte table inside upper2, searched linearly (cmp ecx, 0x7530) and then dereferenced (mov rax, [rax]); left behind by the belt move it would search the middle of the player array and dereference a player field as a pointer. The 0x7530 bound is deliberately not raised: the table cannot grow without room after it, so players past 30000 simply are not in it.)"},
